sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 3, docs/reference/development-containers.md#create): every new Instance is a ZFS clone of the Project's default Instance on its Node, with a clone of its database. Built for the Nodes of the build list. The kind and its step names follow docs/cli/instance/create.mmd; the intent's `container.clone` marks a clone. The Project's first default Instance is container/create-default.mmd; when the charts move into place, it becomes the first-default branch of this chart.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:create
  %% kind: instance.create
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant C as Container<br/>via incus exec
  CLI->>GW: instance:create<br/>PROJECT NODE NAME
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:create PROJECT NODE NAME`
  %%> - syntax: `<project> <node> <name> [--root=PATH] [--domain=HOST] [--branch=BRANCH] [--database-server=SLUG]`
  Note over GW: Validate, reserve Instance<br/>address · T3 port · .env
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has node access to the target Node, an active `app-dev` Node
  %%> - a Project with `nested_fleet` on is admitted only as a container in the nested Incus project: `instance.nested_fleet_host_unavailable` (409) when the Node has nested-fleet hosting off, `instance.nested_fleet_container_required` (409) when the Node is not on the build list or the result is a host checkout, both before any record; the clone is a copy of its default, in the same Incus project
  %%> - the Project's `default` Instance runs in a container on this Node, is active and has a seed snapshot, else `instance.default_missing`
  %%> - Conn is enabled, and the model router has its guard, else `operation.kind_unavailable`
  %%> - a database on a Database server clones on the default's server; another server refuses `instance.database_clone_unsupported`
  %%> - a nested-fleet Project: the Node has the nested-fleet switch, else the placement rule refuses
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the Instance is reserved with its runtime record: container name, bridge address, the lowest free T3 port from 3800 and the default as clone source
  %%> - `.env` is rendered from the Project's env template; it, the placeholder model key and a repository read token go to the vault
  %%> - each attachment of the default marked shared is attached to the clone as it is (same connection, prefix and network, still shared) before `.env` renders, so `.env` holds its keys and the container intent its network path
  %%> - the clone workspace reads one private JSON vault value with `.env`, the Process environment files and the names of the keys the clone owns, of the default's connection keys, of its credential keys and of the shared connections' keys, and the default's Route host with the clone's; SSH stdin takes the whole value
  %%> - a task is recorded with the full intent and `container.clone`
  %%> - a retained create retry records the Project's current development Processes in this admission transaction; changed definitions update their records, removed definitions remove theirs
  %%> - each Process takes its desired state from the default's copy of the same definition: stopped on the default stays stopped (installed, not started, startable by `process:start`); failed, absent or running runs
  Note over GW: Commit, push copies<br/>queue start · answer 202
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  GW->>SW: Start run from queue<br/>operation-instance-create
  par isolated container job · native progress per phase
    SW->>N: Stage clone helpers<br/>native clone-input
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - stages the release's helpers and intent from stdin in a private folder for this run; later phases run its launcher by path
    %%> - scripts and intent never fill the SSH command; the next phase keeps the repository credential on its own stdin
    SW->>N: Clone default container<br/>native clone-container
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the copy supplies the full root disk device (type, path, pool and size), whether the seed inherits it or stores it locally
    %%> - `incus copy` of the default container's snapshot `seed-<commit>`, a ZFS clone; a stopped default needs no start
    %%> - the copy gets its own bridge address and ACL, and the proxy device `t3`: NAT from the Node's WireGuard address and the T3 port to T3's port 3773
    %%> - the container's ACL lets the Node's Caddy reach port 8080, WireGuard peers reach port 3773, and the container reach its database server's port
    %%> - UFW: a route rule admits WireGuard peers to T3, below a deny for the task VM range; a rule admits the container to its database server's port
    %%> - a default with a remote Node service target: writes the base `NO_PROXY` files into the stopped copy before its first start, so units start without the default's hosts
    %%> - starts the copy: nftables, `hidepid` and the image's units start; T3 does not, because `/etc/orbit/instance` does not exist yet
    %%> Mail:
    %%> - the same launch applies the exact SMTP path before the four root-owned mail units; no separate mail playbook or step
    %%> - two IPv4 loopback sockets forward 1025 and 2525; foreign units or listeners skip setup without stopping their Process
    %%> On mail failure:
    %%> - keep a mail warning and continue workspace, T3 and registration; mail:update remains the repair command
    %%> Branch:
    %%> - fetches the Instance's branch into the Node's mirror with the read token, or creates it at the seed commit; the token stays on the Node
    opt nested-fleet clone with a Club key
      SW->>C: Deliver the Club key<br/>native clone-club-key
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - SSH stdin into the copy's /run (a tmpfs, never a snapshot); a new key restarts the nested Gateway's Swamp serve
      %%> - the result's `nested_fleet_club_key` is what this step did; a clone that skips it says `missing`
      %%> On failure:
      %%> - `instance.nested_club_key_not_tmpfs` or `instance.nested_club_key_delivery_failed`; the workspace phase does not run
    end
    opt clone of a nested-fleet default
      SW->>C: Start the inner fleet<br/>clone-fleet · fleet_check · fleet_resume
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - waits for the inner Incus and checks the fleet rules, then starts the three nested containers and the operator tunnel `wg-nested`
      %%> - waits for the same Doctor check a proof uses: the nested Gateway is healthy and its three agents are online
      %%> - only an intent with `fleet` runs it; every other clone skips it, and the workspace phase waits for it or its skip
      %%> Why:
      %%> - the seed holds a stopped, ready fleet, so a clone builds and converges nothing
      %%> - the clone's first start drops the copied boot links, so the tunnel comes from this step, not from a unit
      %%> On failure:
      %%> - `instance.container_fleet_drift`, `instance.container_fleet_check_failed` or `instance.container_fleet_resume_failed`; `error.detail` says why (the Doctor body for a readiness wait); the container is kept for a retry
    end
    opt database on a Database server
      SW->>N: Create the database<br/>child operation-database-create
      %%> What it does, through the database family:
      %%> - creates the Instance's owner and an empty database on the default's server
      SW->>N: Clone the default database<br/>docker exec · admin login
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - PostgreSQL: refuses new connections to the default database and ends its sessions, then `CREATE DATABASE … TEMPLATE`, and gives the clone's objects to the new owner
      %%> - a cleanup that always runs allows connections to the default database again
      %%> - MySQL: a dump of the default database restored into the new one
      %%> Runs beside the clone step: Swamp starts both at once.
    end
    opt Valkey target on the default
      SW->>N: Create the clone's Valkey user<br/>child operation-database-create
      %%> What it does, through the database family:
      %%> - one ACL user on the default's Valkey server with the default user's commands except FLUSHDB and its index, but only the keys `orbit_instance_<id>_*` and no channels
      %%> - attached under the default's prefix, so `.env` gets the connection keys, and for Laravel `<PREFIX>_PREFIX` and `HORIZON_PREFIX` under that key prefix
      %%> - the container's ACL and UFW admit the server's port; no data is copied
      SW->>N: Check the Valkey login<br/>docker exec · owner login
      %%> Runs beside the clone step. A default with more than one Valkey target, or one without an Orbit-made user, or one whose user grants pub/sub, refuses `instance.database_clone_unsupported`.
    end
    par workspace beside agent and T3
    SW->>C: Prepare the workspace<br/>native clone-workspace
    %%> Why beside: agent and T3 never write the workspace; T3 runs Git with `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, so it takes no Git lock; the join below checks both
    %%> When: after the copy, the Club key, the fleet start and the database steps
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - pushes the branch in as a bundle and checks it out in `/srv/workspace`; the group, setgid bits and default ACLs come with the clone
    %%> - after the checkout it checks the branch and commit, then writes the root-owned mark `/var/lib/orbit/workspace-checkout` with the Instance id and commit; when the mark already names this Instance, a retry skips the fetch and checkout, so the branch never moves and the result's commit stays the mark's
    %%> - writes `.env` for `orbit` with group `work`: the default's file from the seed, with the clone's own connection keys, the keys of the connections it shares with its default and `APP_URL`, without the default's other connection and Reverb keys or a copy of its credentials; `APP_KEY` stays the default's, because the cloned data is encrypted with it
    %%> - a copied value that points at the default's Route host (its Route without a web root) points at the clone's Route host; the rest of the value stays
    %%> - prints only the names of the copied, dropped, rewritten and shared keys; the result carries them as `environment`
    %%> - before Process start, prepares and fetches Node as orbit in this same phase; an inherited private recipe is kept, an old store is converted once even without Processes, so a later Node consumer can install its pin
    %%> No setup steps:
    %%> - the default Instance installed the dependencies and migrated; a later lockfile change is installed in the workspace
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes the shared FrankenPHP Caddyfile and unit, then restarts it as `orbit`; only the Node's bridge peer with `X-Forwarded-Proto: https` sets PHP's HTTPS scheme, port and resolved client IP
    %%> - starts use nonblocking systemd jobs, then a bounded readiness check for each running unit; container Process units order after `network.target`
    and agent and T3 beside the workspace
    SW->>C: Prepare the agent<br/>native clone-agent
    %%> When: after the copy and the Club key; it does not wait for the fleet start, the workspace or the database steps
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes the placeholder key for `agent`, and the Claude Code and Codex settings that point at the model forwarder
    %%> - links `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` and `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` of `agent` to the note of the Project type
    %%> - writes `/etc/orbit/instance`, owned by root and readable by all
    SW->>C: Start T3<br/>native clone-t3
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - T3 starts for the first time and creates its identity; the T3 project `/srv/workspace` is added as `agent`
    %%> Check:
    %%> - waits up to 30 s for `/.well-known/t3/environment`, else `instance.t3_unready`
    %%> Why its own lock: the clone steps share one Swamp lock; agent and T3 take `ic-clone-t3-…`, so they run beside the workspace
    end
    SW->>C: Register the T3 server<br/>native clone-register
    %%> When: the join; the sessions check waits for T3 and the workspace, because it checks the branch, the checkout mark and every Process unit
    %%> On a failed workspace: no sessions check, no registration; the container stop below still runs
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - see conn/environment-renew.mmd: the sessions go to the vault, and the step checks the environment id and scopes
    %%> - an inactive required unit refuses with `instance.container_process_inactive`; copy its structured public refusal even when sessions failed, skip registration, and retain the unit states in the Operation
  and independent Route job · no depth link
    opt web-serving Project
      SW->>N: Make, sign Route key<br/>child route-create-csr
      SW->>N: Create the Route<br/>child operation-route-create
      %%> What it adds:
      %%> - the same steps as `route:create`, with the signed certificate, then a TLS handshake check; no HTTP request waits for app startup
      %%> - the Node's Caddy proxies the Route to FrankenPHP at the container's bridge address
      %%> - the Route job waits only for its CSR; a separate job prevents depth scheduling from delaying the container phases
      %%> - the prepared Route skips workspace ACL and environment writes; the container job owns those
    end
  end
  alt all steps pass in budget
    C-->>SW: T3 and site answer
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Record Instance, T3 server<br/>active · registered
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Instance, its runtime and its Route become active; the runtime records the default Instance it came from
    %%> - the Conn layer records the T3 server from the result; its Node is the container's Node and it names the Instance
    %%> - the result's `processes_stopped` names the Processes left stopped, as on the default
    %%> - the receipt includes when T3 answered, its sessions passed, and the Route TLS probes passed
  else Instance already created
    Note over GW: Skipped — already created<br/>instance.exists
  else a step fails or the budget ends
    C--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or timeout
    SW->>N: Attempt Route withdrawal<br/>child route-withdraw
    %%> Caddy publication:
    %%> - on the Node, wait at most 5 s for the publish lock; compare the composed-from SHA-256 with the live file, then validate, rename and reload under that lock
    %%> - a changed base refuses with `caddy.composed_from_live_mismatch`; a busy lock refuses with `caddy.publish_busy`; the live Caddyfile stays unchanged and the normal failure path runs
    %%> When:
    %%> - only when the run published it
    SW->>N: Attempt container stop<br/>incus stop
    %%> What stays:
    %%> - the reservation, runtime, and any container, workspace, owned databases, test databases and role stay until the owner acts
    %%> - a refused retry removes none of them; stop and Route withdrawal are attempted; failed compensation leaves its step failed
    %%> - shared service endpoint records and rules may remain even after destroy until endpoint lifecycle work is live
    %%> - failed and cancelled creates, including cancellation before work starts, report retained_for_retry, the same create command with a new idempotency key, and forced destroy
    %%> Cleanup:
    %%> - remove the private clone folder after success or failure, even if staging or the first launch failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step, error_code
    %%> - an inactive Project Process adds recovery.retry.requires=project_process_definition; fix or remove its definition before retry
    Note over GW: Record the failure
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again; it resumes on the same container and database
    %%> - a resume never moves a branch this Instance checked out: commits on it stay
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
